2604:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c **** /**
2605:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @brief      Enters LP accel motion interrupt mode.
2606:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  The behavior of this feature is very different between the MPU6050 and the
2607:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  MPU6500. Each chip's version of this feature is explained below.
2608:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2609:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n MPU6050:
2610:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n When this mode is first enabled, the hardware captures a single accel
2611:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  sample, and subsequent samples are compared with this one to determine if
2612:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  the device is in motion. Therefore, whenever this "locked" sample needs to
2613:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  be changed, this function must be called again.
2614:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2615:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n The hardware motion threshold can be between 32mg and 8160mg in 32mg
2616:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  increments.
2617:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2618:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n Low-power accel mode supports the following frequencies:
2619:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n 1.25Hz, 5Hz, 20Hz, 40Hz
2620:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2621:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n MPU6500:
2622:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n Unlike the MPU6050 version, the hardware does not "lock in" a reference
2623:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  sample. The hardware monitors the accel data and detects any large change
2624:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  over a short period of time.
2625:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2626:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n The hardware motion threshold can be between 4mg and 1020mg in 4mg
2627:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  increments.
2628:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2629:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n MPU6500 Low-power accel mode supports the following frequencies:
2630:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n 1.25Hz, 2.5Hz, 5Hz, 10Hz, 20Hz, 40Hz, 80Hz, 160Hz, 320Hz, 640Hz
2631:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2632:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n\n NOTES:
2633:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n The driver will round down @e thresh to the nearest supported value if
2634:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  an unsupported threshold is selected.
2635:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n To select a fractional wake-up frequency, round down the value passed to
2636:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @e lpa_freq.
2637:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n The MPU6500 does not support a delay parameter. If this function is used
2638:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  for the MPU6500, the value passed to @e time will be ignored.
2639:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n To disable this mode, set @e lpa_freq to zero. The driver will restore
2640:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  the previous configuration.
2641:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2642:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @param[in]  thresh      Motion threshold in mg.
2643:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @param[in]  time        Duration in milliseconds that the accel data must
2644:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *                          exceed @e thresh before motion is reported.
2645:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @param[in]  lpa_freq    Minimum sampling rate, or zero to disable.
2646:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @return     0 if successful.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\chen\AppData\Local\Temp\cc50WfpY.s 			page 200


2647:BSP/MPU6050/eMPL/inv_mpu.c ****  */
